      "text": "\"Hindi po ito masasabing walang krimen. The mere fact na sinabi niya ito in public, to the public, pertaining to a particular person. It is already covered by Safe Spaces Act,\" Palace Press Officer Claire Castro said as she rebuked remarks made by a lawmaker that drew fierce backlash, warning that publicly expressed “fantasies” about women may constitute sexual harassment under the law.\n\nRepublic Act 11313 or the Safe Spaces Act penalizes gender-based sexual harassment in streets, public spaces, workplaces and online platforms.\n\nQuezon City 4th District Rep. Bong Suntay has come under fire for saying during Tuesday’s hearing of the House justice committee on the impeachment of Vice President Sara Duterte that he felt “desires” after seeing actress Anne Curtis in person.\n\nFULL STORY: https://t.co/u414NGJOys",
